From 81d18c82d246b4cc9f855ef80e3792b21600386f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:37:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: keep the shared content filter lists up to date

Web apps may ask for maintained ad and tracker lists such as EasyList by
name. Kodi now keeps those lists itself: advancedsettings.xml names them
and their URLs under <webapps><contentfilterlists>, with EasyList and
EasyPrivacy predefined, and CWebFilterLists stores them in the profile
and hands them to the web client. A list is fetched with a conditional
request once the kernel reports the system clock synchronised, as TLS
needs a valid clock, and again once a day. Until then a change of the
clock, or a web app asking for a list Kodi never had, makes it look
again.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
